# ==================================================
# CardioVision AI — environment template
#
# Copy to .env and edit. Nothing here is required: the app runs with every
# value at its default. .env is gitignored; this file is not.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# There is no dotenv loader in the backend, on purpose — one fewer dependency,
# and one fewer place a password can be silently picked up from. Export the
# variables yourself, or source the file:
#
#     set -a && . ./.env && set +a
#     cardiovision serve
# ==================================================


# --------------------------------------------------
# OPERATOR ACCOUNT
#
# One fixed account. The defaults exist so the app is usable out of the box,
# not because they are secure: the password is compared in constant time but it
# is a single shared secret over plain HTTP, which protects a shared
# workstation from a passer-by and nothing more.
#
# Change both together. Setting only the username leaves the default password.
# --------------------------------------------------

# CARDIOVISION_USER=medexpert
# CARDIOVISION_PASSWORD=1111


# --------------------------------------------------
# PROJECT ROOT
#
# Where models/ and data/ live. Detected by walking up from the installed
# package looking for pyproject.toml or models/, which is correct for a
# checkout and for `pip install -e .`. Set this when the package is installed
# non-editable, or when the weights live on another volume — a wrong root
# surfaces as "checkpoint not found", not as anything mysterious.
# --------------------------------------------------

# CARDIOVISION_HOME=/absolute/path/to/CardioVision-AI


# --------------------------------------------------
# CORS
#
# Comma-separated origins allowed to call the API. Defaults to the Vite dev
# server on both spellings of localhost:
#
#     http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173
#
# Add an origin here when serving the built frontend from somewhere else. A
# wildcard is not accepted, and would not work anyway — the browser refuses
# credentialed requests against `*`.
# --------------------------------------------------

# CARDIOVISION_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173


# --------------------------------------------------
# SKIP MODELS AT STARTUP
#
# Any truthy value (1, true, yes, on) keeps that model out of memory. Skipping
# MedGemma saves ~8.6 GB and most of the cold-start time, which is the
# difference between a 3-second restart and a 90-second one while iterating on
# the imaging code.
#
# `cardiovision serve --skip medgemma` sets these for you; repeat --skip for
# more than one.
#
# A skipped model is reported as unavailable by /api/health, and its panel in
# the UI says so, rather than the frontend pretending it is there.
# --------------------------------------------------

# CARDIOVISION_SKIP_ECHO=1
# CARDIOVISION_SKIP_CCTA=1
# CARDIOVISION_SKIP_ECG=1
# CARDIOVISION_SKIP_MEDGEMMA=1


# --------------------------------------------------
# FRONTEND
#
# The API base URL is compiled into the bundle at build time, so it is a Vite
# variable rather than one the backend reads. Put it in frontend/.env.local.
# Defaults to http://127.0.0.1:8000.
# --------------------------------------------------

# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
